  <div id="lessonContent">
    <h2>1. What Will We Build?</h2>
    <p>Today we build a <b>real working calculator</b> - Just like the one on your phone. It can add, subtract, multiply, divide, clear, delete, and show history.</p>
    <p>This project uses everything you learned: <b>HTML</b> for buttons, <b>CSS</b> for design, <b>JS Variables</b> for display, <b>Functions</b> for buttons, <b>DOM</b> to update screen, <b>Events</b> for clicks, <b>eval()</b> to calculate.</p>
    <div class="note"><b>How a Calculator Works - 3 Steps:</b> 1. User clicks buttons - Numbers join together as text - "5" + "+" + "3" = "5+3". 2. User clicks = - JavaScript calculates "5+3". 3. Answer shows on display - "8".</div>
    <h2>2. LIVE DEMO - Try Your Calculator</h2>
    <p>Use it - It really works. Try 12 + 8 = , 50 - 20, 7 x 6:</p>
    <div class="demo-card">
      <div class="calc">
        <div class="calc-display">
          <div class="calc-history" id="calcHistory"></div>
          <div class="calc-main" id="calcDisplay">0</div>
        </div>
        <div class="calc-grid">
          <button class="calc-btn clear" onclick="calcClear()">C</button>
          <button class="calc-btn" onclick="calcBack()">⌫</button>
          <button class="calc-btn op" onclick="calcPress('%')">%</button>
          <button class="calc-btn op" onclick="calcPress('/')">÷</button>
          <button class="calc-btn" onclick="calcPress('7')">7</button>
          <button class="calc-btn" onclick="calcPress('8')">8</button>
          <button class="calc-btn" onclick="calcPress('9')">9</button>
          <button class="calc-btn op" onclick="calcPress('*')">×</button>
          <button class="calc-btn" onclick="calcPress('4')">4</button>
          <button class="calc-btn" onclick="calcPress('5')">5</button>
          <button class="calc-btn" onclick="calcPress('6')">6</button>
          <button class="calc-btn op" onclick="calcPress('-')">−</button>
          <button class="calc-btn" onclick="calcPress('1')">1</button>
          <button class="calc-btn" onclick="calcPress('2')">2</button>
          <button class="calc-btn" onclick="calcPress('3')">3</button>
          <button class="calc-btn op" onclick="calcPress('+')">+</button>
          <button class="calc-btn zero" onclick="calcPress('0')">0</button>
          <button class="calc-btn" onclick="calcPress('.')">.</button>
          <button class="calc-btn eq" onclick="calcEqual()">=</button>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p style="margin-top:12px;color:#64748b;font-size:13px">Tip: You can also use your keyboard - Type numbers and press Enter for =</p>
    </div>
    <h2>3. Step 1 - HTML - Display + Buttons</h2>
    <div class="code-box"><code>
<span class="tag">&lt;input</span> <span class="attr">id</span>=<span class="val">"display"</span> <span class="attr">readonly</span><span class="tag">&gt;</span> <span class="comment" style="color:#94a3b8">&lt;!-- Shows numbers --&gt;</span><br><br>
<span class="tag">&lt;button</span> <span class="attr">onclick</span>=<span class="val">"press('7')"</span><span class="tag">&gt;</span><span class="text">7</span><span class="tag">&lt;/button&gt;</span><br>
<span class="tag">&lt;button</span> <span class="attr">onclick</span>=<span class="val">"press('8')"</span><span class="tag">&gt;</span><span class="text">8</span><span class="tag">&lt;/button&gt;</span><br>
<span class="tag">&lt;button</span> <span class="attr">onclick</span>=<span class="val">"press('+')"</span><span class="tag">&gt;</span><span class="text">+</span><span class="tag">&lt;/button&gt;</span><br>
<span class="tag">&lt;button</span> <span class="attr">onclick</span>=<span class="val">"calculate()"</span><span class="tag">&gt;</span><span class="text">=</span><span class="tag">&lt;/button&gt;</span><br>
<span class="tag">&lt;button</span> <span class="attr">onclick</span>=<span class="val">"clearDisplay()"</span><span class="tag">&gt;</span><span class="text">C</span><span class="tag">&lt;/button&gt;</span>
    </code></div>
    <h2>4. Step 2 - CSS - Grid for Buttons</h2>
    <div class="code-box"><code>
<span class="text">.calc { width: 300px; background: #0f172a; padding: 15px; border-radius: 15px; }</span><br>
<span class="text">.calc-display { background: white; padding: 15px; text-align: right; font-size: 28px; border-radius: 10px; }</span><br>
<span class="text">.calc-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr 1fr 1fr; gap: 8px; }</span><br>
<span class="text">.calc-btn { padding: 15px; font-size: 20px; border-radius: 10px; border: none; cursor: pointer; }</span>
    </code></div>
    <p><b>Grid Trick:</b> <code>grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr 1fr 1fr</code> makes 4 equal columns - Perfect for calculator buttons.</p>
    <h2>5. Step 3 - JavaScript - 4 Functions Only</h2>
    <div class="code-box"><code>
<span class="text">let display = document.getElementById("display");</span><br><br>
<span class="comment" style="color:#94a3b8">// 1. Add button value to display</span><br>
<span class="text">function press(value) {</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">if (display.value === "0") { display.value = value; }</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">else { display.value = display.value + value; }</span><br>
<span class="text">}</span><br><br>
<span class="comment" style="color:#94a3b8">// 2. Calculate - eval() solves the text as math</span><br>
<span class="text">function calculate() {</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">try {</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">let result = eval(display.value); // eval("5+3") = 8</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">display.value = result;</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">} catch (error) {</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">display.value = "Error";</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">}</span><br>
<span class="text">}</span><br><br>
<span class="comment" style="color:#94a3b8">// 3. Clear - Empty display</span><br>
<span class="text">function clearDisplay() { display.value = "0"; }</span><br><br>
<span class="comment" style="color:#94a3b8">// 4. Backspace - Remove last character</span><br>
<span class="text">function backspace() {</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">display.value = display.value.slice(0, -1);</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">if (display.value === "") { display.value = "0"; }</span><br>
<span class="text">}</span>
    </code></div>
    <h2>6. What is eval()?</h2>
    <p><b>eval() = Evaluate - Solve Text as Math.</b> If you give it a string "5+3", it returns 8. If you give it "10*2", it returns 20.</p>
    <div class="code-box"><code>
<span class="text">console.log(eval("5 + 3")); // 8</span><br>
<span class="text">console.log(eval("10 * 2")); // 20</span><br>
<span class="text">console.log(eval("100 / 4")); // 25</span><br>
<span class="text">console.log(eval("50 - 20")); // 30</span>
    </code></div>
    <div class="note"><b>Warning:</b> eval() is easy for learning, but in real big apps, developers do not use eval() for user input because it can run any code. For this lesson and small projects, eval() is OK. In Lesson 40 we will learn a safer way without eval().</div>
