<span class="tag">&lt;!DOCTYPE html&gt;</span><br>
<span class="tag">&lt;html&gt;</span><br>
<span class="tag">&lt;head&gt;</span> <span class="tag">&lt;style&gt;</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">.calc { width:300px; background:#0f172a; padding:15px; border-radius:15px; margin:20px auto; }</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">input { width:100%; padding:15px; font-size:26px; text-align:right; border-radius:10px; border:none; margin-bottom:10px; }</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">.grid { display:grid; grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr 1fr 1fr; gap:8px; }</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">button { padding:15px; font-size:20px; border-radius:10px; border:none; cursor:pointer; }</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">.eq { background:#16a34a; color:white; }</span><br>
<span class="tag">&lt;/style&gt;</span> <span class="tag">&lt;/head&gt;</span><br>
<span class="tag">&lt;body&gt;</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="tag">&lt;div</span> <span class="attr">class</span>=<span class="val">"calc"</span><span class="tag">&gt;</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="tag">&lt;input</span> <span class="attr">id</span>=<span class="val">"display"</span> <span class="attr">value</span>=<span class="val">"0"</span> <span class="attr">readonly</span><span class="tag">&gt;</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="tag">&lt;div</span> <span class="attr">class</span>=<span class="val">"grid"</span><span class="tag">&gt;</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="tag">&lt;button</span> <span class="attr">onclick</span>=<span class="val">"press('7')"</span><span class="tag">&gt;</span><span class="text">7</span><span class="tag">&lt;/button&gt;</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="tag">&lt;button</span> <span class="attr">onclick</span>=<span class="val">"press('8')"</span><span class="tag">&gt;</span><span class="text">8</span><span class="tag">&lt;/button&gt;</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="tag">&lt;button</span> <span class="attr">onclick</span>=<span class="val">"press('9')"</span><span class="tag">&gt;</span><span class="text">9</span><span class="tag">&lt;/button&gt;</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="tag">&lt;button</span> <span class="attr">onclick</span>=<span class="val">"press('+')"</span><span class="tag">&gt;</span><span class="text">+</span><span class="tag">&lt;/button&gt;</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="tag">&lt;button</span> <span class="attr">onclick</span>=<span class="val">"clearDisplay()"</span><span class="tag">&gt;</span><span class="text">C</span><span class="tag">&lt;/button&gt;</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="tag">&lt;button</span> <span class="attr">onclick</span>=<span class="val">"calculate()"</span> <span class="attr">class</span>=<span class="val">"eq"</span><span class="tag">&gt;</span><span class="text">=</span><span class="tag">&lt;/button&gt;</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="tag">&lt;/div&gt;</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="tag">&lt;/div&gt;</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="tag">&lt;script&gt;</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">let display = document.getElementById("display");</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">function press(v) { if (display.value === "0") display.value = v; else display.value += v; }</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">function calculate() { try { display.value = eval(display.value); } catch(e) { display.value = "Error"; } }</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">function clearDisplay() { display.value = "0"; }</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="tag">&lt;/script&gt;</span><br>
<span class="tag">&lt;/body&gt;</span> <span class="tag">&lt;/html&gt;</span>
    </code></div>
    <h2>8. Homework - Make It Better</h2>
    <p>In Playground, add these to your calculator:</p>
    <p>1. Add all buttons 0-9, + - * / . = C ⌫ - Full calculator like demo<br>2. Add History - After =, show "5+3 = 8" in a small line above display<br>3. Add Keyboard Support - When user presses number keys on keyboard, call press() - Hint: use <code>document.addEventListener("keydown")</code></p>
    <div class="box"><b>Remember:</b> Calculator = Display + Buttons | press(value) = Add to display | eval("5+3") = 8, Solves text as math | calculate() = eval + try/catch | clearDisplay() = Reset to 0 | backspace() = slice(0, -1) remove last | Grid 1fr 1fr 1fr 1fr = 4 columns for buttons | try/catch = If error, show "Error" not crash</div>
